<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <%- include("./partials/_brand_head") %>
    <%- include("./partials/_fonts") %>

    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>Privacy Policy - CreatorOS</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">

    <style>
        .privacy-page {
            min-height: 100vh;
            padding: 48px 20px 72px;
        }

        .privacy-container {
            width: min(960px, 100%);
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        .privacy-header {
            margin-bottom: 32px;
        }

        .privacy-badge {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 8px;
            padding: 7px 12px;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            border: 1px solid currentColor;
            border-radius: 999px;
            font-size: 12px;
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: 0.08em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        .privacy-header h1 {
            margin: 0 0 12px;
            font-family: "Space Grotesk", sans-serif;
            font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
            line-height: 0.98;
            letter-spacing: -0.04em;
        }

        .privacy-intro {
            max-width: 760px;
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 1rem;
            line-height: 1.75;
            opacity: 0.78;
        }

        .privacy-meta {
            margin-top: 14px;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            opacity: 0.6;
        }

        .privacy-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
            gap: 18px;
        }

        .privacy-card {
            padding: 26px;
            border: 1px solid rgba(127, 127, 127, 0.25);
            border-radius: 18px;
            background: rgba(127, 127, 127, 0.04);
        }

        .privacy-card.full-width {
            grid-column: 1 / -1;
        }

        .privacy-card h2 {
            margin: 0 0 14px;
            font-family: "Space Grotesk", sans-serif;
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            line-height: 1.2;
        }

        .privacy-card h3 {
            margin: 20px 0 8px;
            font-size: 1rem;
        }

        .privacy-card p {
            margin: 0 0 12px;
            line-height: 1.7;
        }

        .privacy-card p:last-child {
            margin-bottom: 0;
        }

        .privacy-card ul {
            margin: 10px 0 0;
            padding-left: 20px;
        }

        .privacy-card li {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
            line-height: 1.65;
        }

        .privacy-card li:last-child {
            margin-bottom: 0;
        }

        .privacy-link {
            text-decoration: underline;
            text-underline-offset: 3px;
        }

        .privacy-back {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 8px;
            margin-top: 34px;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        .privacy-back:hover {
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        @media (max-width: 720px) {
            .privacy-page {
                padding: 32px 16px 52px;
            }

            .privacy-grid {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            }

            .privacy-card.full-width {
                grid-column: auto;
            }

            .privacy-card {
                padding: 22px;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <main class="privacy-page">
        <div class="privacy-container">

            <header class="privacy-header">
                <div class="privacy-badge">
                    Privacy &amp; Data
                </div>

                <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

                <p class="privacy-intro">
                    CreatorOS respects your privacy and is committed to being transparent
                    about the information the application collects, how it is used, and
                    the services that may process it.
                </p>

                <p class="privacy-meta">
                    This policy describes the current data-handling behavior of CreatorOS.
                </p>
            </header>

            <section class="privacy-grid">

                <!-- 1. Information collected -->
                <article class="privacy-card full-width">
                    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

                    <p>
                        Depending on the features you use, CreatorOS may process information
                        associated with your account and your use of the application.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Account information:</strong>
                            name, email address, authentication provider information,
                            and related account identifiers.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <strong>Creator profile information:</strong>
                            information you choose to provide for your creator profile,
                            such as an alias and biography.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <strong>Authentication and security information:</strong>
                            authentication tokens, email-verification information,
                            two-factor authentication information, and password-change
                            timestamps.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <strong>Subscription information:</strong>
                            subscription status, plan information, billing-period
                            information, and identifiers associated with payment
                            processing.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <strong>Integration information:</strong>
                            information required to connect supported services such as
                            Google Calendar.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <strong>Security and request information:</strong>
                            certain technical information, such as IP address and
                            user-agent information, may be recorded for security-related
                            operations such as password-reset requests.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </article>

                <!-- 2. How information is used -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS uses information to provide, maintain, and secure its
                        features.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>Provide and authenticate user accounts.</li>
                        <li>Provide creator and content-management features.</li>
                        <li>Manage subscriptions and billing status.</li>
                        <li>Support booking and calendar integrations.</li>
                        <li>Send account-related and transactional emails.</li>
                        <li>Protect the application against abuse and unauthorized access.</li>
                        <li>Process account deletion and related requests.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>

                <!-- 3. Cookies and local storage -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>3. Cookies &amp; Local Storage</h2>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS uses browser storage technologies to support
                        authentication, security, and application functionality.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            Authentication sessions may use HTTP cookies containing
                            authentication tokens.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            A temporary cookie may be used during two-factor
                            authentication.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            CreatorOS uses a security cookie to help protect
                            state-changing requests against cross-site request forgery.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            Some application data and preferences may be stored in
                            browser local storage.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            The contributor login flow may store an authentication token
                            and user information in local storage.
                        </li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Some values stored through CreatorOS's secure-storage utility
                        are encrypted before being written to local storage.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 4. Authentication -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>4. Authentication &amp; Account Data</h2>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS supports password-based authentication, Google
                        Sign-In, contributor authentication, and optional
                        two-factor authentication.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Passwords for local accounts are hashed using bcrypt rather
                        than being stored as plain-text passwords.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Authentication sessions use JSON Web Tokens (JWTs). Depending
                        on the authentication flow, a token may be maintained through
                        an HTTP-only cookie or returned to a client application.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Email verification and password-reset links use temporary
                        security tokens with limited validity periods.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 5. Google -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>5. Google Services</h2>

                    <h3>Google Sign-In</h3>

                    <p>
                        If you choose to sign in with Google, CreatorOS receives
                        information provided through Google's authentication flow,
                        including your Google account identifier, email address,
                        display name, and profile image when available.
                    </p>

                    <h3>Google Calendar</h3>

                    <p>
                        If you connect Google Calendar, CreatorOS may use the
                        integration to create and manage calendar events associated
                        with bookings.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Calendar events created through this integration may contain
                        event titles, descriptions, attendee names and email
                        addresses, and meeting start and end times.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS stores the authorization information required to
                        maintain the Google Calendar connection.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 6. Stripe -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>6. Payment &amp; Subscription Services</h2>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS uses Stripe for subscription checkout and billing
                        management when Stripe is configured for the deployment.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        During checkout, information such as your email address and
                        CreatorOS account identifier may be provided to Stripe.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS receives subscription-related information from
                        Stripe, such as subscription status, Stripe customer and
                        subscription identifiers, pricing information, billing-period
                        information, and cancellation status.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Payment processing is handled through Stripe's checkout
                        infrastructure.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 7. Email -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>7. Email Services</h2>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS uses an email delivery service configured by the
                        deployment to send transactional messages.
                    </p>

                    <p>These messages may include:</p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>Account verification emails.</li>
                        <li>Password-reset emails.</li>
                        <li>Account-deletion confirmation emails.</li>
                        <li>Collaboration invitation emails.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        The email service configuration may vary between deployments.
                        CreatorOS does not assume a particular email provider.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 8. AI -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>8. AI Features</h2>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS includes AI-assisted creator features. When the
                        OpenAI integration is enabled, user-provided prompts and up to
                        the most recent four conversation-history messages may be
                        processed through OpenAI to generate responses and suggestions.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Before prompts are sent to OpenAI, CreatorOS attempts to
                        redact certain sensitive patterns, including email addresses,
                        bearer tokens, API keys, and card-number patterns.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        If OpenAI is unavailable or not configured, CreatorOS can use
                        a local processing fallback for supported AI features.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        The application code does not establish that AI conversations
                        are permanently retained, so this policy does not make a
                        broader retention claim about AI conversations.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 9. Instagram -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>9. Instagram Profile Lookups</h2>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS may retrieve publicly available Instagram profile
                        information when you request an Instagram profile lookup.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Retrieved profile information may be temporarily cached for
                        up to 30 minutes to reduce repeated requests and improve
                        performance.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        The profile-lookup functionality described here is designed
                        to retrieve public profile information and does not establish
                        access to private Instagram account content.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 10. Security -->
                <article class="privacy-card full-width">
                    <h2>10. Security</h2>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS implements multiple technical measures intended to
                        protect accounts and application data.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            Local account passwords are hashed using bcrypt.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            Authentication cookies are configured as HTTP-only, and
                            production deployments use secure cookies.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            SameSite cookie policies are used to reduce cross-site
                            request risks.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            CSRF tokens are used to protect state-changing requests.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            Login and password-reset attempts are subject to
                            protection against repeated failed requests.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            Two-factor authentication is available for supported
                            accounts.
                        </li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        No method of electronic storage or transmission can be
                        guaranteed to be completely secure. Security measures may
                        also change as the project evolves.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 11. Retention and deletion -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>11. Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS retains account information for as long as necessary
                        to provide the application's features and manage the account.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Users can request account deletion through the account
                        settings flow. Account deletion includes a 30-day grace
                        period before permanent deletion is carried out.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Temporary security information, such as verification,
                        password-reset, authentication, and cached integration data,
                        has limited validity or retention according to the relevant
                        application flow.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        This policy does not make claims about retention in external
                        providers' backups or systems where the application's source
                        code does not establish those retention periods.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 12. User rights -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>12. Your Choices &amp; Rights</h2>

                    <p>
                        Depending on your use of CreatorOS and applicable law, you may
                        have rights concerning your personal information.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>Review or update information associated with your account.</li>
                        <li>Request deletion of your CreatorOS account.</li>
                        <li>Disconnect supported third-party integrations.</li>
                        <li>Request information about how your data is handled.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        To make a privacy-related request, contact the CreatorOS team
                        through the support or contact channel provided by the project.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 13. Changes -->
                <article class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>13. Changes to This Policy</h2>

                    <p>
                        CreatorOS may update this Privacy Policy when the application's
                        features, integrations, or data-handling practices change.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Updated versions will be published on this page. We encourage
                        users to review this page periodically for changes.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <!-- 14. Contact -->
                <article class="privacy-card full-width">
                    <h2>14. Contact</h2>

                    <p>
                        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how
                        CreatorOS handles information, please contact the CreatorOS
                        maintainers through the project's designated support or
                        contact channel.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        For account-specific requests, please provide enough
                        information for the maintainers to understand and process
                        your request without unnecessarily including sensitive
                        information.
                    </p>
                </article>

            </section>

            <a href="/" class="privacy-back">
                ← Back to CreatorOS
            </a>

        </div>
    </main>
</body>
</html>